1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:02,272
Your build worked yesterday.

2
00:00:02,272 --> 00:00:03,221
Today it fails,

3
00:00:03,221 --> 00:00:04,740
and you changed nothing.

4
00:00:04,740 --> 00:00:07,967
A library you never asked for just changed version.

5
00:00:08,517 --> 00:00:11,205
That is the world of transitive dependencies.

6
00:00:11,205 --> 00:00:13,236
Libraries pull in other libraries,

7
00:00:13,236 --> 00:00:17,178
and sometimes two of them want different versions of the same one.

8
00:00:17,728 --> 00:00:20,507
Today you learn to read the dependency tree,

9
00:00:20,507 --> 00:00:21,580
see the conflict,

10
00:00:21,580 --> 00:00:23,412
understand how Maven chooses,

11
00:00:23,412 --> 00:00:24,107
and fix it.

12
00:00:24,657 --> 00:00:26,427
Then you solve a conflict yourself.

13
00:00:26,977 --> 00:00:28,029
One honest note.

14
00:00:28,029 --> 00:00:31,251
My recording computer cannot reach Maven Central,

15
00:00:31,251 --> 00:00:35,327
so the demos use two tiny libraries I built in a local folder.

16
00:00:35,327 --> 00:00:39,009
The commands and the tree are exactly what you will see.

17
00:00:40,559 --> 00:00:43,418
A direct dependency is one you write in your pom.

18
00:00:43,968 --> 00:00:47,360
A transitive dependency is one your dependency needs.

19
00:00:47,360 --> 00:00:48,576
You never wrote it.

20
00:00:48,576 --> 00:00:50,112
Maven brings it for you.

21
00:00:50,662 --> 00:00:53,234
Your project asks for lib A and lib B.

22
00:00:53,234 --> 00:00:54,656
Lib A needs you till,

23
00:00:54,656 --> 00:00:55,468
version one.

24
00:00:55,468 --> 00:00:56,889
Lib B needs you till,

25
00:00:56,889 --> 00:00:57,702
version two.

26
00:00:58,252 --> 00:01:02,134
Only one version can go on the class path. So Maven must choose.

27
00:01:02,684 --> 00:01:07,932
That clash is a version conflict. It is common, and it is quiet, until something breaks.

28
00:01:09,982 --> 00:01:11,166
How Maven chooses.

29
00:01:11,166 --> 00:01:12,678
Rule one: nearest wins.

30
00:01:12,678 --> 00:01:16,361
The version closest to your project in the tree is used.

31
00:01:16,911 --> 00:01:21,028
Rule two: if two are the same distance, the first one declared wins.

32
00:01:21,578 --> 00:01:22,378
In our case,

33
00:01:22,378 --> 00:01:24,245
you till is two levels away,

34
00:01:24,245 --> 00:01:25,179
through lib A,

35
00:01:25,179 --> 00:01:26,846
and also two levels away,

36
00:01:26,846 --> 00:01:27,780
through lib B.

37
00:01:27,780 --> 00:01:28,180
A tie.

38
00:01:28,180 --> 00:01:29,780
Lib A is declared first,

39
00:01:29,780 --> 00:01:31,114
so version one wins.

40
00:01:31,664 --> 00:01:33,697
The newest version does not win.

41
00:01:33,697 --> 00:01:34,777
The nearest does,

42
00:01:34,777 --> 00:01:35,602
or the first.

43
00:01:35,602 --> 00:01:37,317
That surprises many people.

44
00:01:37,867 --> 00:01:42,966
Version one is chosen, but our code needs a method that only exists in version two.

45
00:01:45,016 --> 00:01:46,765
Three ways to fix a conflict.

46
00:01:47,315 --> 00:01:47,563
One.

47
00:01:47,563 --> 00:01:48,924
Dependency management.

48
00:01:48,924 --> 00:01:51,275
Pin the version for the whole project,

49
00:01:51,275 --> 00:01:52,079
in one place.

50
00:01:52,079 --> 00:01:53,502
This is the best habit.

51
00:01:54,052 --> 00:01:58,937
Two. An exclusion. Tell Maven: from this dependency, leave that library out.

52
00:01:59,487 --> 00:01:59,888
Three.

53
00:01:59,888 --> 00:02:01,222
Declare it yourself,

54
00:02:01,222 --> 00:02:01,822
directly.

55
00:02:01,822 --> 00:02:03,891
A direct dependency is nearest,

56
00:02:03,891 --> 00:02:04,625
so it wins.

57
00:02:04,625 --> 00:02:05,025
Quick,

58
00:02:05,025 --> 00:02:06,293
but easy to forget.

59
00:02:06,843 --> 00:02:11,173
We will use the first one, dependency management. Then prove it with the tree.

60
00:02:13,223 --> 00:02:16,380
Go to the demo project. Type: CD, demo.

61
00:02:16,930 --> 00:02:25,805
Print the tree. Type: mvn -B dependency:tree | grep 'jar:' | cut -c8-

62
00:02:25,935 --> 00:02:29,967
Maven reads every pom, direct and transitive. A few seconds.

63
00:02:35,517 --> 00:02:36,887
Read it like folders.

64
00:02:36,887 --> 00:02:38,387
Our project at the top.

65
00:02:38,387 --> 00:02:38,778
Lib A,

66
00:02:38,778 --> 00:02:39,626
and under it,

67
00:02:39,626 --> 00:02:40,474
you till one.

68
00:02:40,474 --> 00:02:41,192
Then lib B.

69
00:02:41,742 --> 00:02:50,659
Now ask for the details. Type: mvn -B dependency:tree -Dverbose | grep omitted | cut -c8-

70
00:02:50,789 --> 00:02:53,669
Verbose mode also lists what Maven left out.

71
00:03:00,219 --> 00:03:00,996
There it is.

72
00:03:00,996 --> 00:03:02,551
You till two point zero,

73
00:03:02,551 --> 00:03:05,206
omitted for conflict with one point zero.

74
00:03:05,206 --> 00:03:06,825
Lib B wanted version two,

75
00:03:06,825 --> 00:03:07,408
and lost.

76
00:03:07,958 --> 00:03:09,725
Focus on one library.

77
00:03:09,725 --> 00:03:17,046
Type: mvn -B dependency:tree -Dincludes=com.cloudcart.lib:util | grep 'jar:' | cut -c8-

78
00:03:17,176 --> 00:03:21,251
Includes keeps only the path to one library. Useful in a big tree.

79
00:03:27,801 --> 00:03:30,852
Only the path to you till. Version one, through lib A.

80
00:03:31,402 --> 00:03:37,802
Now the build. Type: mvn -B -q compile 2>&1 | head -4

81
00:03:37,932 --> 00:03:39,852
Quiet mode, so only errors show.

82
00:03:46,402 --> 00:03:46,996
It fails.

83
00:03:46,996 --> 00:03:48,251
Cannot find symbol,

84
00:03:48,251 --> 00:03:48,648
shout.

85
00:03:48,648 --> 00:03:51,752
That method is only in you till two point zero.

86
00:03:51,752 --> 00:03:53,932
The conflict is now a real error.

87
00:03:54,482 --> 00:03:58,877
Here is the fix, as a block. Type: cat dm.xml

88
00:03:59,007 --> 00:04:00,481
Dependency management,

89
00:04:00,481 --> 00:04:03,094
with you till pinned to two point zero.

90
00:04:03,094 --> 00:04:04,166
No jar is added.

91
00:04:04,166 --> 00:04:05,841
It only sets the version,

92
00:04:05,841 --> 00:04:07,583
wherever you till appears.

93
00:04:08,133 --> 00:04:16,496
Insert it into the pom. Type: sed -i '/<\/properties>/r dm.xml' pom.xml

94
00:04:16,626 --> 00:04:18,823
Print the tree again. Type: mvn -B dependency:tree | grep 'jar:' | cut -c8-

95
00:04:21,553 --> 00:04:23,132
Same command as before.

96
00:04:28,682 --> 00:04:33,524
You till is now two point zero, under lib A. Lib A did not change. The pin did.

97
00:04:34,074 --> 00:04:39,109
Build again. Type: mvn -B -q compile && echo built

98
00:04:39,239 --> 00:04:40,220
Almost there.

99
00:04:46,770 --> 00:04:49,373
Built. Conflict found, understood, and fixed.

100
00:04:50,923 --> 00:04:51,774
Your lab task.

101
00:04:51,774 --> 00:04:55,361
Lab eighty-eight gives you a build with a version conflict.

102
00:04:55,361 --> 00:04:57,003
Lab check judges your work.

103
00:04:57,553 --> 00:04:59,609
It lives at git hub dot com,

104
00:04:59,609 --> 00:05:01,077
slash it dash waves,

105
00:05:01,077 --> 00:05:02,766
slash dev ops dash A I,

106
00:05:02,766 --> 00:05:03,573
in academy,

107
00:05:03,573 --> 00:05:03,867
lab,

108
00:05:03,867 --> 00:05:05,702
lab eighty-eight dot S H.

109
00:05:06,252 --> 00:05:08,022
One: before you fix anything,

110
00:05:08,022 --> 00:05:11,927
save the verbose tree lines with omitted into conflict dot text.

111
00:05:12,477 --> 00:05:14,865
Two: pin you till to two point zero,

112
00:05:14,865 --> 00:05:17,188
with a dependency management block.

113
00:05:17,188 --> 00:05:19,112
Do not delete lib A or lib B.

114
00:05:19,662 --> 00:05:23,224
Three: M V N clean package must end in build success.

115
00:05:23,774 --> 00:05:26,562
Four: save the new tree into tree dot text.

116
00:05:26,562 --> 00:05:28,961
It must show you till two point zero,

117
00:05:28,961 --> 00:05:30,388
and no one point zero.

118
00:05:30,938 --> 00:05:33,764
Five: write one sentence in why dot text,

119
00:05:33,764 --> 00:05:36,934
about the rule Maven used to pick version one.

120
00:05:36,934 --> 00:05:38,381
Use the word nearest,

121
00:05:38,381 --> 00:05:39,002
or first.

122
00:05:39,552 --> 00:05:41,833
Install a J D K and Maven first.

123
00:05:41,833 --> 00:05:42,689
Then lab up,

124
00:05:42,689 --> 00:05:43,402
lab check,

125
00:05:43,402 --> 00:05:44,329
and lab down.

126
00:05:44,329 --> 00:05:47,466
The shortcut file is shortcuts eighty-eight.

127
00:05:49,516 --> 00:05:51,585
Pass or fail. You need all six.

128
00:05:52,135 --> 00:05:53,949
Five pass lines in lab check.

129
00:05:54,499 --> 00:05:57,592
You can read a dependency tree, direct and transitive.

130
00:05:58,142 --> 00:06:01,619
You can state the two rules: nearest wins, then first declared.

131
00:06:02,169 --> 00:06:04,431
You can name three ways to fix a conflict.

132
00:06:04,981 --> 00:06:07,946
You can find a conflict with dash capital D verbose.

133
00:06:08,496 --> 00:06:10,416
lab down, nothing left behind.

134
00:06:10,966 --> 00:06:12,267
To pass, all six.

135
00:06:14,317 --> 00:06:17,154
Your turn, in your own Ubuntu virtual machine.

136
00:06:17,704 --> 00:06:19,795
One: lab up, and read the task file.

137
00:06:20,345 --> 00:06:24,377
Two: save the conflict into conflict dot text, before any fix.

138
00:06:24,927 --> 00:06:27,487
Three: add the dependency management block.

139
00:06:28,037 --> 00:06:30,341
Four: build, and save tree dot text.

140
00:06:30,891 --> 00:06:33,344
Five: write why dot text, and lab check.

141
00:06:33,894 --> 00:06:36,476
Six: lab down, and prove nothing is left.

142
00:06:37,026 --> 00:06:38,860
Pause the video, and begin now.

143
00:06:54,410 --> 00:06:55,285
Quick check.

144
00:06:55,835 --> 00:06:57,733
What is a transitive dependency?

145
00:06:58,283 --> 00:07:00,161
Which version wins in a conflict?

146
00:07:00,711 --> 00:07:02,695
Name two ways to fix a conflict.

147
00:07:03,245 --> 00:07:04,973
Which flag shows what was omitted?

148
00:07:05,523 --> 00:07:08,808
Objective covered: M C ten, objective four.

149
